 "about": "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later. The fixed roster of fictional names for layer H scenarios (BENCHMARK-V2.md P10, E-25; AUTHORING-SPEC.md \"History scenarios\"). Amended 16 October 2026, decision 176: it replaces the forbidden-names blocklist, which could not tell a company from an ordinary word and was never complete. Precedent: RedlineBench fixes its parties (AgentCo, LargeCo, GiantCo); Harvey LAB keeps its matters synthetic-only and checks that by review, not by a word filter. Use: the counterparty under review and our own side are the parties the clean document already names (documentParties, by clean document and side), so the current document and the record agree; every other counterparty is drawn from `companies` by hash of the scenario id (lib/scenarios.mjs assignOthers, called by author.mjs scenarioPlan), never reused across one author's ten scenarios; covering-email senders are `people` at an assigned `.example` domain. apply-scenarios.mjs checks counterparty names and aliases, matter names and covering-email senders exactly against the scenario's assigned entries (case-insensitive, Unicode-normalised); free text (edits, covering text) is checked by the validators' real-name question, not by a word list. The names were invented for this roster; none is meant to be a real company or person. Frozen with the scenarios.",
